  "title": "Enheduanna",
  "summary": "Enheduanna was a daughter of Sargon of Akkad, named high priestess of the moon god Nanna at Ur. Poems and hymns, including the Temple Hymns, are credited to her and were copied by scribes for generations. A disc carrying her name was found at Ur. Her dates are approximate and tradition surrounds her career.",
